    {
      "number": 34,
      "file": "slide-34.webp",
      "section": "progress",
      "hasNotes": true,
      "notes": "For this project, we built four failure scenarios to verify the monitoring-based auto-recovery (self-healing) flow.\nEach scenario was designed around a failure that could realistically happen in a production environment, with the goal of verifying this flow: Prometheus Alert → AlertManager → Recovery Controller → automatic recovery → status normalization.\nFor each scenario, we also verified the Slack notification, the recovery log entry, and whether the Grafana dashboard returned to normal.\nNginxDown restarts the service automatically once nginx_up drops to 0.\nNginxExporterDown restarts the exporter itself.\nHighCPU terminates the load process once CPU exceeds 80%.\nHighMemoryUsage runs a memory-cleanup command once memory exceeds 70%.\nWe'll walk through each of these scenarios briefly, then show them actually running in the demo video.\""
    },
